;; M7 sub-slice (a): recursive (same-SCC) min lattice -- dist reads dist
;; through the cycle 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 1, so the lattice head is recursive and
;; M6L's contributor machinery historically refused to retain state for it.
;; Today ANY signed deletion in the cone falls back to clear-and-rerun
;; (route rerun); M7 sub-slice (b) flips regressions to the
;; stored-contributor repair fixpoint.  Sub-slice (a) pins the substrate
;; only: same-SCC contributor retention and rank witnesses, certified equal
;; to a forced fresh recount, with routing unchanged.
;;
;; The deletion scenario (batch-:edge,2,3,5) exercises, per key:
;;   dist(1,3): 15 -> 100     regression to a RETAINED LOSER (direct edge);
;;   dist(1,4): 16 -> 17      likewise (losers 17 and 30 both retained);
;;   dist(1,1): 17 -> 102     regression through a REPLACEMENT cascade
;;                            around the cycle (new value, derived from the
;;                            regressed dist(1,3));
;;   dist(2,1)/(2,2)/(2,3):   all contributors die -> present-to-absent.
;;
;; Rank witnesses stamp per CONTRIBUTOR row (the lattice's tuples), at the
;; physical semi-naive round of first derivation: the (+ D W) compute
;; stages through a temp, so depths stride 2 (direct edge 1, one hop 3,
;; two hops 5).  Losers subsumed by the lattice merge before reaching the
;; delta (e.g. (1,4)->30) carry no forward stamp -- sub-slice (b) derives
;; those on demand during repair.

lattice (cost (min int #:floor 0))
table (edge int int int)
table (dist int int cost)

rule (edge X Y W) --> (dist X Y W)
rule (dist X Y D) (edge Y Z W) --> (dist X Z (+ D W))
